  "id": "Compound::DB00709 - Gene::6582",
  "verbalization": "Lamivudine appears to interact with Slc22a2 through a series of molecular and functional pathways that involve the Slc22 family of transporters. The evidence suggests that Lamivudine binds to Slc22a3, which is involved in the transport of dopamine and quaternary ammonium groups across cellular membranes. This binding may trigger a functional interaction where Slc22a3 participates in the transport process, ultimately leading to the participation of Slc22a2 in the same activity. The shared involvement of Slc22a2 in these transport processes implies a potential functional relationship between Lamivudine and Slc22a2, possibly through a mechanism involving transporter-mediated transport or modulation of transporter activity. The evidence is consistent with a model where Lamivudine influences the function of Slc22a2 via its interaction with Slc22a3, highlighting a possible role in cellular transport regulation.",
